1. d4 c5 2. dxc5 e6 3. b4 a5 4. c3 axb4 5. cxb4 Qf6 6. Na3 Rxa3 7. Rb1 Rxa2 {
"...and wins." Source: Melbourne Leader, 19 Oct 1907; but The Field, 17 Aug
1907, records the opening as a 'Sicilian' with the comment: "Kelly fell into a
trap and lost a piece in the opening. In spite of it he kept Blackburne at bay
for a considerable time and the latter only won the game after an adjournment.
" (51 moves)} 0-1

